{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkdTZYWr5a2mNiNSxzpy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`contract/claim.compact` is written and compiles cleanly. I ran `compact compile` and it exited with code 0.\n\n- **Public key:** `publicKey(sk)` is an exported pure circuit that returns `persistentHash([pad(32, \"claim:pk:\"), sk])`.\n- **Claim:** `claim()` reads `secretKey()` and computes a nullifier, `persistentHash([pad(32, \"claim:nf:\"), sk])`. It asserts the nullifier isn't already in the `nullifiers` set, inserts it, and increments the `claims` counter. A second claim with the same secret key fails with \"Already claimed\".\n- **Witnesses:** `secretKey()` is the only one.\n\n**Privacy:** the nullifier uses a different domain tag from the public key. Without the secret key, nobody can compute it from a public key. Nobody can check whether a given public key appears in the ledger. Storing the public key itself in the set would have broken this.\n\n**Limitation:** the public key and nullifier are both deterministic hashes of the same secret key. Someone who knows the secret key can link the two, but that person already is the user."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":145,"cache_read_input_tokens":21774,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":145},"output_tokens":373,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6212f57d-25ee-4295-bcce-436c53a83db3","uuid":"58c62dcd-ecd0-4b1c-a5b9-bda2bdde6127","timestamp":"2026-11-05T23:13:34.999Z","request_id":"req_011CgkdTZL7ZXqLrGUQYo5Az"}
